 12: /**
 13:  * The game master panel's state.
 14:  *
 15:  * It owns no game state and grants nothing: everything here builds the same
 16:  * `/line` a game master would type and hands it to `Social.sendChat`, which
 17:  * sends it as ordinary chat. The server decides whether to run it - it re-reads
 18:  * `CharacterStatus` on every command it receives
 19:  * (`ChatMessageCommandProcessor`), so a player who forced this window open gets
 20:  * exactly what they would get from typing: nothing.
 21:  *
 22:  * Sends are queued because `sendChat` refuses a second line inside
 23:  * `CHAT_COOLDOWN_MS` and says so only by returning false. Without the queue a
 24:  * quick second click would be swallowed with no sign anything was lost.
 25:  *
 26:  * No member here may be named after one on `Object.prototype`.
 27:  * `makeAutoObservable` matches its overrides with `key in overrides`, which
